        "original_id": "293d4215-3415-5f93-b2d8-d65daa10c9fc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Howard\n- Organizations: Baltimore and Ohio Railroad\n- Places: Maryland, Baltimore, Sandy Hook\n- Roles: American mechanical engineer\n\nFacts:\n- William Howard was an American mechanical engineer who lived from 1793 to 1834.\n- William Howard was one of the first people to work for the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad.\n- At first, the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad was located entirely in the state of Maryland.\n- The Baltimore and Ohio Railroad originally ran west from the port of Baltimore to Sandy Hook.",
